ntdll: give ARM64EC translation a thread stack it can survive on.

In ARM64EC translation under FEX, exception dispatches push ARM64EC_NT_XCONTEXT
frames (3.3 KB each), and guest x64 code executes on the CHPE v2 emulator stack.
The default CHPE stack was hardcoded to only 256 KB (0x40000), which overflows
instantly during Electron / V8 JIT recursive execution and CreateWindowEx.
Raising chpev2_stack_size and the virtual_alloc_thread_stack floor to 8 MB
provides ample headroom.

This patch used to carry a second, unrelated change: it clamped any pure
MEM_RESERVE larger than 8 GB down to 8 GB and reported success, so that V8's
1.47 TB pointer-compression cage would not fail outright on a 39-bit-VA kernel.
That half is removed, because it did not do what it claimed.

V8 does not merely commit inside the cage it asked for -- it *validates* the
reservation it was given, rejects one of the wrong size, releases it, and asks
again at a smaller size. It has a fallback ladder, and it walks it: measured on
device, 1.5 TB, then 516 GB, 260 GB, 132 GB, 68 GB, 64 GB, 36 GB, 16 GB, three
attempts a rung.

Reporting success for a request that was not honoured breaks that ladder. V8
can never descend past a rung it believes it cleared, so it loops: 36,043
clamped reservations in one session, 59,601 attempts at a single size, and an
Electron renderer pinned at 100% of a core that never paints a window. Each
rejected 8 GB release also made FEX invalidate 8 GB of translations --
524,288 times -- which is the JIT thrash that made this look like an emulator
bug for a day.

Failing honestly is what the ladder needs, and the address space was never the
obstacle: every rung from 48 GB down fits in the 512 GB a 39-bit kernel gives.
The clamp was not protecting V8 from a small address space. It was preventing
V8 from finding the size that fits in it.
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
index 9ee9239947f..76dbf7f71f5 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
@@ -1247,7 +1247,11 @@ NTSTATUS init_thread_stack( TEB *teb, ULONG_PTR limit, SIZE_T reserve_size, SIZE
     if (is_arm64ec())
     {
         CHPE_V2_CPU_AREA_INFO *cpu_area;
-        const SIZE_T chpev2_stack_size = 0x40000;
+        /* Vessel: Expand CHPE v2 emulator stack from 256 KB to at least 8 MB
+         * (or image MaximumStackSize). Guest x64 code under FEX runs on this
+         * emulator stack, and 256 KB overflows immediately during deep recursion,
+         * V8 compilation, and SEH dispatching. */
+        const SIZE_T chpev2_stack_size = max( (SIZE_T)8 * 1024 * 1024, max( reserve_size, commit_size ) );
 
         /* emulator stack */
         if ((status = virtual_alloc_thread_stack( &stack, limit_4g, 0, chpev2_stack_size, chpev2_stack_size, FALSE )))
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index b18593e0f19..eb4468e23e9 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -4791,7 +4791,10 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_alloc_thread_stack( INITIAL_TEB *stack, ULONG_PTR limit_low, UL
     if (!commit_size) commit_size = main_image_info.CommittedStackSize;
 
     size = max( reserve_size, commit_size );
-    if (size < 1024 * 1024) size = 1024 * 1024;  /* Xlib needs a large stack */
+    /* Vessel: ARM64EC translation frames and V8/Electron recursive workloads require
+     * a generous stack (at least 8 MB). Default 256KB-1MB stacks overflow quickly under
+     * ARM64EC_NT_XCONTEXT exception dispatching. */
+    if (size < 8 * 1024 * 1024) size = 8 * 1024 * 1024;
     size = ROUND_SIZE( 0, size, granularity_mask );
 
     server_enter_uninterrupted_section( &virtual_mutex, &sigset );
